      "message": "Will all this work correctly if the chromeos_pstore driver is disabled (so the ramoops info is present in ACPI but the host kernel doesn\u0027t do anything with it?)\n\nIf not, we should probably wrap all this in an `#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CHROMEOS_PSTORE)`?\n\nHmm... BTW what about the fact that we enable it as a module (so it is not loaded yet when pKVM is initialized, it is only loaded later during boot)?\n\n...Also, any reason why put all this code here between `early_pkvm_relax_cpu_bugs_parse_cmdline()` and `early_pvmfw_parse_cmdline()` (which both parse kernel command line options, while this code doesn\u0027t)?\n\nI\u0027d put them, for example, between `pkvm_firmware_rmem_clear()` and `vmx_pkvm_init()`. (It\u0027s not like this ramoops stuff is more important than the pvmfw stuff?)",
