      "message": "\u003e Will all this work correctly if the chromeos_pstore driver is disabled (so the ramoops info is present in ACPI but the host kernel doesn\u0027t do anything with it?)\n\u003e \n\u003e If not, we should probably wrap all this in an #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CHROMEOS_PSTORE)?\n\u003e \n\u003e Hmm... BTW what about the fact that we enable it as a module (so it is not loaded yet when pKVM is initialized, it is only loaded later during boot)?\n\nI thought about it - it should be fine as is: here we only parse this info, while we log the error to the ramoops console only when proper SIG is detected (see aosp/4032092 which among other things performs a runtime signature verification to ensure it is writing to a correctly initialized pstore buffer.). And this is true only if this driver is enabled (even as a module). Otherwise this info is just parsed and any logging to ramoops is skipped.\n\n\u003e .. I\u0027d put them, for example, between pkvm_firmware_rmem_clear() and vmx_pkvm_init(). (It\u0027s not like this ramoops stuff is more important than the pvmfw stuff?)\n\nOk. No specific reason - I\u0027ve just put the whole new chunk at the begining but after early_param\u0027s - moved it as suggested.",
