      "writtenOn": "2026-04-16T20:16:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would be nice to move this logic into a separate function (e.g. `pkvm_ramoops_init()`?\n\nAlso, any reason why do this at the very beginning, even before `pkvm_firmware_rmem_init()`? There is a reason why `pkvm_firmware_rmem_init()` is done at the very beginning: we want to know the pvmfw address and size before even checking if pKVM is enabled, in order to clear pvmfw from memory if pKVM is disabled. While in the ramoops case, we don\u0027t need to parse ramoops info from ACPI if pKVM is disabled?",
